A thread made ready with a deadline before the turn's request waits for the timer rather than taking the processor.
The earliest deadline would not run first, and a driver woken by its interrupt would wait for the turn of a spinner.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits with a deadline before the turn's request
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1359,7 +1359,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
         /* Its end is the timer's to mark. */
         core->wake_stale = true;
     }
-    return core->run_queue != 0 && due_before(run_earliest(core)->deadline, own->deadline);
+    return false;
 }
 
